# PART 57 — NUMERICAL IMPLEMENTATION CONTRACT

## 1. Number classification

Every behavioral number is classified as one of:

LOCKED — architectural requirement.
DEFAULT — initial implementation value; change requires a versioned decision.
DERIVED — calculated from other parameters; not independently configured.
ADAPTIVE — computed at runtime from current state.
TUNABLE — deliberately benchmarked/configured.
OPEN — not yet established; provisional default must be explicit.

The coding model must never silently invent a LOCKED or DEFAULT value.

## 2. Master audio parameters

Initial DEFAULTS:

sample_rate = 48000 Hz
channels = 2
sample_format = float32

If the input device uses another sample rate, the system either operates at
that rate or performs an explicit versioned sample-rate conversion. Silent
resampling is prohibited.

## 3. Device buffer

Initial DEFAULT:

device_buffer = 256 samples

At 48 kHz this is 5.333 ms. Actual device buffer size and actual sample rate
must be recorded at runtime because hardware, drivers, buffers and algorithmic
processing all contribute to latency. citeturn0search6turn0search0

## 4. Fast analysis hop

DEFAULT:

fast_hop = 256 samples

At 48 kHz:

fast_period = 5.333 ms

The fast path must not fall behind this cadence.

## 5. Short FFT

DEFAULT:

short_fft_size = 1024
short_fft_hop = 256
window = Hann

At 48 kHz:

window_duration = 21.333 ms
frequency_bin_spacing = 46.875 Hz

FFT size is separate from device buffer size. Larger windows provide finer
frequency discrimination at the cost of temporal resolution/latency. citeturn0search7turn0search2

## 6. Long FFT

DEFAULT:

long_fft_size = 4096
long_fft_hop = 1024

At 48 kHz:

window_duration = 85.333 ms
frequency_bin_spacing = 11.719 Hz

The long FFT must not block the critical fast path.

## 7. Fast-loop deadline

Initial engineering target:

p99 fast-loop compute time <= 50% of fast_period

At 48 kHz / 256 samples:

p99 compute target <= 2.667 ms

Deadline misses must be counted and logged.

## 8. End-to-end event latency

Initial targets:

p50 perception-to-event <= 20 ms
p95 <= 30 ms
p99 <= 50 ms

These are engineering acceptance targets, not claims about every hardware
configuration. Buffer size directly affects when realtime audio commands can
be consumed. citeturn0search1

## 9. Context windows

DEFAULTS:

short_observation_context = 100 ms
medium_observation_context = 500 ms
tracking_context = 2 s

These are evidence-retention contexts, not object lifetimes.

## 10. Object persistence

DEFAULTS:

candidate_confirmation_window = 50 ms
prediction_horizon = 100 ms
recovery_window = 250 ms
uncertain_window = 500 ms
archive_delay = 2000 ms

One missing observation must not terminate identity.

## 11. Match thresholds

Initial normalized-score defaults:

strong_match >= 0.80
candidate_match >= 0.55
reject_match < 0.40

Scores from 0.40 through 0.549... are ambiguous and must not automatically
produce a confident assignment.

Thresholds are TUNABLE and require benchmark validation.

## 12. Match hysteresis

DEFAULTS:

promotion_margin = 0.10
demotion_margin = 0.10
minimum_assignment_duration = 30 ms

An established identity receives hysteresis protection.

## 13. Confidence decay

Initial half-life defaults when unsupported by new evidence:

measurement_confidence_half_life = 100 ms
prediction_confidence_half_life = 150 ms
identity_confidence_half_life = 500 ms
semantic_confidence_half_life = 2000 ms

The decay function must be explicit and versioned.

## 14. Masking

DEFAULTS:

mask_attack = 20 ms
mask_release = 150 ms

Masking changes perceptual confidence/salience. It does not delete physical
identity, history, or observations already retained as evidence.

## 15. Grouping tolerances

Initial DEFAULTS:

temporal_group_tolerance = 30 ms
strong_temporal_group_tolerance = 10 ms
frequency_overlap_tolerance = 0.15 normalized band distance

These values are TUNABLE.

## 16. Split/merge hysteresis

DEFAULTS:

merge_confirmation = 3 consecutive compatible updates
split_confirmation = 3 consecutive incompatible updates
minimum_split_duration = 30 ms
minimum_merge_duration = 30 ms

A single contradictory frame must not cause structural identity change.

## 17. Prediction error

DEFAULTS:

prediction_warning_threshold = 0.25 normalized error
